    "summary": "East Inner Gopura. Muang Tam, Thailand, 11th century. \nThis partially-restored Shaiva temple, sitting below Phnom Rung, lacks inscription but has been dated by stylistic analysis to the 11th century. The eastern inner gopura is viewed here from between the inner and outer enclosures; in the photo foreground (right and left edges) one can see two naga railings, the corners of large ponds which are dug out between the enclosures.",
